  "primary_unit": "ton",
  "why": "Erection productivity is dominated by piece count per tonne, not just tonnage - primary members (columns, main beams, trusses) erect fast per tonne while secondary steel (bracing, purlins, girts, sag rods) is light and piece-heavy and erects much slower per tonne. Splitting the tonnage into primary and secondary gives a realistic blended rate for a crane-served erection crew.",
